Conclusion

For the uniform-audit baselines B2 and B3 with refund-and-ban enforcement and no bonds, against
honest rivals whose play does not depend on the focal identity and with re-entry before the next
allocation, free replacement removes the ban’s continuation cost. At the fixed parameters, the
prescribed D2+H3 searches yield a lower measured gain for R3 than for B3 on every sampled market,
but the registered gain-and-efficiency comparison passes on only three of six fresh markets, all three
qualified by search flags. R3 and the development-selected verified-history comparator are pooledequivalent within the pre-set margin in the six sampled markets under both Q1 families, which are
close to one test; with the frozen searches the difference varies in sign across markets (with the
doubled searches and each rule’s strongest family it is positive on all six), and this analysis does not
establish the ordering for the neighbourhood. At the headline market, the selected unconstrained
welfare attacks yield gross efficiency of about 0.840 against all three core rules and earn less than the
truthful reference against R3 and C∗ . The registered W1 search found no profitable welfare attack
(gross efficiency near 0.997); exploratory mixtures of a welfare attack and a profitable attack reach
lower efficiency at non-negative estimated gain, so it supplies no efficiency bound for randomised
policies. These conclusions concern frozen searches and references, with interval calibration admitted
on development fixtures. The record of both tests, including the original failure, the amendments,
the deviations, and the failed predictions, will be released with the paper.
Availability. The paper artifact will have its own release commit and archive hash. It identifies
the frozen evaluation code by the signed tag protocol-v2 and preserves the original tagged-code
report. It contains the code, the tuned files, all records of both tests (including incomplete, failed,
and cut cells), the market generator, the block headers, the released H4 bundle, and the deviation evidence, and, separately dated, the decision-stability re-evaluation, the exploratory post hoc
analyses with the per-seed evaluation and training inputs of the lottery analysis, the predictionscoring correction with its regression test, the inference audit, and the paper sources. One command (docs/revision/deviation/reproduce_deviation.py) checks the artifact against the tag
and reproduces the second test’s report under the disclosed configuration substitution; the paper’s
second-test tables and figures are regenerated from the tagged report, the disclosed stability output, and the exploratory post hoc and audit outputs by the scripts in docs/revision/paper-v2,
docs/revision/posthoc, and docs/revision/audit, and the first test’s records and verdict are in
the release as recorded in October 2026.

